<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Carmagnole</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">first sung in August <a href="/years/1792">1792</a>; added to in <a href="/years/1830">1830</a>, <a href="/years/1848">1848</a>, <a href="/years/1863">1863</a>–64 and <a href="/years/1882">1882</a>–83</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;La Carmagnole&quot; is a French song created and made popular during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a>, together with a wild dance of the same name that may have come into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> with the Piedmontese. It was first sung in August 1792, and new verses were added in the revolutionary years of 1830, 1848, 1863–64 and 1882–83. Its authors are not known.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>&quot;<b>La Carmagnole</b>&quot; is a French song created and made popular during the French Revolution, together with a wild dance of the same name that may have come into France with the Piedmontese.</blockquote><a href="/songs/carmagnole">La Carmagnole</a></li></ul></section>
